{"type":"standard","title":"Khakas language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Khakas language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q33575","titles":{"canonical":"Khakas_language","normalized":"Khakas language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Khakas language</span></span>"},"pageid":3287533,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Khakas_Ethno-Language.png/330px-Khakas_Ethno-Language.png","width":330,"height":248},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/Khakas_Ethno-Language.png","width":3000,"height":2250},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1350790266","tid":"3521cd5a-3f7f-11f1-b490-2571ff3d7ddd","timestamp":"2026-04-24T01:45:01Z","description":"Northeastern Turkic language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khakas_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khakas_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khakas_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Khakas_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khakas_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Khakas_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khakas_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Khakas_language"}},"extract":"Khakas, also known as Xakas, is a Turkic language spoken by the Khakas, who mainly live in the southwestern Siberian Republic of Khakassia, in Russia. The Khakas number 61,000, of whom 29,000 speak the Khakas language. Most Khakas speakers are bilingual in Russian.","extract_html":"<p><b>Khakas</b>, also known as <b>Xakas</b>, is a Turkic language spoken by the Khakas, who mainly live in the southwestern Siberian Republic of Khakassia, in Russia. The Khakas number 61,000, of whom 29,000 speak the Khakas language. Most Khakas speakers are bilingual in Russian.</p>"}